  "body_markdown": "Skip to content\n\nDental Implants\n\nDental Implant Surgery\n\nAll-on-4 Dental Implants\n\nFixed Teeth vs. Removable\n\nCost & Compare\n\nDental Implant FAQ\n\nAesthetics\n\nCosmetic Dentistry\n\nPorcelain Veneers\n\nDental Crowns & Bridges\n\nSmile Makeover\n\nTeeth Whitening\n\nTreatments\n\nSedation Dentistry\n\nOral Surgery\n\nEmergency Dentistry\n\nConditions We Treat\n\nWhat To Expect\n\nPatient Center\n\nInsurance & Financing\n\nSmile Gallery\n\nWho We Are\n\nWhy Choose Us\n\nMeet Dr. Esam Nahlah\n\nMeet The Team\n\nVideo Library\n\nPatient Stories\n\nFor Doctors\n\nReferral Form\n\nContact Us\n\nBlog\n\nCurrent Patients\n\nTysons Corner: (703) 448-3312\n\nAlexandria: (703) 940-5410\n\nNew Patients\n\nTysons Corner: (571) 619-9442\n\nAlexandria: (571) 410-3430\n\nBook now\n\n\n## Book Now\n\n\n\n## Book Now\n\n\n\n## How Many Missing Teeth Can Dental Implants Replace?\n\n\nNovember 21, 2023\n\n\n#### Share This Post\n\n\nA dental implant is a gold standard tooth replacement option that is composed of a dental implant post, an abutment, and a prosthesis. The dental implant post is made to act like a natural tooth root, the abutment is the connector piece, and the prosthesis is what gives patients a natural and better-looking new smile.\n\nDepending on each person’s specific smile, dental implants in McLean, VA can be used to replace any number of missing teeth. Here is more on how many teeth dental implants can replace.\n\n\n## The Number Of Missing Teeth Dental Implants In McLean, VA Can Replace\n\n\nDental implants can replace any number of missing teeth. Whether people have one missing tooth, several missing teeth, or a full arch of missing teeth, dental implants can restore the look, function, and health of their smile for years to come. As long as people have enough jawbone density to support their new smile, dental implants can reliably and predictably replace missing teeth.\n\nFor those who don’t have enough jawbone density to replace their missing teeth, they can first be treated with a bone grafting procedure. A bone grafting procedure will give the patient a stable foundation for their new smile to be placed on.\n\n\n## The Types Of Dental Implants In McLean, VA I Can Replace My Missing Teeth With\n\n\nHere are the specific types of dental implant options people’s missing teeth can be replaced with.\n\n\n### Single Dental Implants:\n\n\nSingle Dental Implants are used when only one tooth is missing. The single dental implant post replaces the root of the missing tooth and supports a custom-made tooth crown (prosthesis). This is the most natural-looking and functional solution for a single missing tooth.\n\n\n### Implant Supported Dentures:\n\n\nImplant Supported Dentures are a great tooth replacement option for those who have missing teeth or are ready to upgrade their smile from traditional dentures. With implant supported dentures, two or more dental implants are used to support a denture.\n\n\n### Full Mouth Dental Implants:\n\n\nFull mouth dental implants are used to replace an entire arch, or arches, of missing teeth. When people are treated with full mouth dental implants, four or more dental implants are strategically placed in the patient’s jawbone so they can securely support the prosthesis.\n\n\n## See Us Now So We Can Replace Your Missing Teeth With Dental Implants\n\n\nNo matter how many missing teeth you have, we have the restorative dental implant options that can transform your smile for years to come. Why wait to improve your smile with us? Get in contact with our doctors, Dr. Esam Nahlah and our exceptional team at our office to schedule an appointment today!\n\nPrevPreviousCan I Upgrade My Smile From Traditional Dentures To Implant Supported Dentures?\n\nNextReady To Learn How Full Mouth Dental Implants Are Cost-Effective?Next\n\n\n#### More To Explore\n\n\n\n### Unlock the Benefits of Dental Implants: Your Best Teeth Replacement Option\n\n\nTooth loss can become an unfortunate reality for many as we age. Thankfully, advancements in dental technology, like dental implants,\n\nRead More »\n\nOctober 26, 2024\n\n\n### Your Comprehensive Guide on Dental Implants: The Best Replacement of Tooth Solution\n\n\nDental implants in McLean, VA are small, and titanium posts are surgically placed in your jawbone underneath your gum line.\n\nOctober 20, 2024\n\n\n## You Are Welcome Here.\n\n\nSchedule your consultation today.\n\nFacebook Instagram Youtube Google\n\n\n#### Contact Us\n\n\nAddresses:\n\nTysons Corner\n\n7901 Jones Branch Dr., Suite 220\n\nMcLean, VA 22102\n\nNew Patients: (571) 619-9442\n\nCurrent Patients: (703) 448-3312\n\nAlexandria\n\n2855 Duke St,\n\nAlexandria, VA 22314\n\nNew Patients: (571) 410-3430\n\nCurrent Patients: (703) 940-5410\n\n\n#### Hours\n\n\nMonday: 8:00am – 5:00pm\n\nTuesday: 8:00am – 5:00pm\n\nWednesday: 8:00am – 5:00pm\n\nThursday: 8:00am – 5:00pm\n\nFriday: 8:00am – 2:00pm\n\nSaturday: Closed\n\nSunday: Closed\n\n\n#### Services\n\n\nAll-On-4® Implants\n\nCrowns & Bridges\n\n\n#### About Us\n\n\nMeet the Doctor\n\nAbout Us\n\nBefore & After Photos\n\n2025 Dr. Nahlah. All rights reserved",
